{
  "tema": 7443,
  "slug": "hay-lo-hay",
  "titulo": "No hay / no lo hay: when the object pronoun can drop",
  "subtitulo": "—¿Hay tortillas? —No, no hay.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "Most verbs need lo, la, los, las to refer back to a noun: —¿Viste a tu mamá? —No, no la vi. But with haber, tener, querer (and often llevar, traer, necesitar) in short answers, the pronoun is usually left out, especially when the noun is unspecific: —¿Hay leche? —No, no hay.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Normal verbs **need** the pronoun: **—¿Llamaste al plomero? —Sí, lo llamé.** (never ~~sí, llamé~~)"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With **haber, tener, querer, llevar, traer, necesitar**, short answers usually **drop** it: **—¿Tienes cambio? —Sí, tengo.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Dropping is most natural when the noun is general or uncountable (**leche, dinero, tiempo**). For a specific known thing, keep it: **—¿Tienes mis llaves? —Sí, las tengo.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Both are correct in many cases; the version without the pronoun sounds more casual."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **hay, tengo, quiero** can stand alone; most verbs can't."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "—¿Hay refrescos en el refri? —No, ==no hay==.",
              "en": "—Are there sodas in the fridge? —No, there aren't."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Hay muchos perros en el parque? —No, ==no hay== tantos.",
              "en": "—Are there lots of dogs in the park? —No, not that many."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Tienes dinero para la pizza? —Sí, ==tengo==.",
              "en": "—Do you have money for the pizza? —Yes, I do."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Quién quiere pozole? —¡Yo ==quiero==!",
              "en": "—Who wants pozole? —I do!"
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Traen monedas para el estacionamiento? —Sí, ==traemos==.",
              "en": "—Do you have coins for parking? —Yes, we do."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Tienes las llaves del carro? —Sí, ==las tengo==.",
              "en": "—Do you have the car keys? —Yes, I have them."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Viste a tu mamá hoy? —No, ==no la vi==.",
              "en": "—Did you see your mom today? —No, I didn't."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
